descriptions:
The project aims to increase access of Uzbekistan’s population to objective & inclusive media content and information by 
a) enhancing the  capacity of selected Uzbek media outlets to produce more objective and inclusive media content;
b)  enhancing the capacity of journalists, journalism students and the wider public on data journalism and identification of ‘fake news’.

The project aims to improve and simplify access to digital public services for all Uzbek citizens, in particular for vulnerable social groups, as well as to improve the effectiveness of public policy design processes to prevent corruption by: 
a) Improving the capacity of Uzbek Government to develop citizen-centric digital transformation strategies for public service delivery;
b) Enhancing operational capacity of Uzbek Government to develop effective regulatory impact assessment (RIA) and anticorruption screening.

Project aims to continue its support to the Government of Uzbekistan to deliver prioritised, co-ordinated and targeted governance reforms by: 
a) Providing MoJ with support on implementation of a selected number of capability review recommendations;
b) Strengthening the capacity of MoJ staff further;
c) Extending its support offer to the Presidential Administration.

The project aims to support the rehabilitation and reintegration services for children in closed educational institutions back into their families and communities by:
a) improving the quality of reintegration services provided to children leaving specialised closed institutions;
b) improving the rehabilitation services to children in these institutions through development and utilisation of individual reintegration and rehabilitation plans.

